; WS2_32.DEF
;
; The functions the Windows 98 SE / Me build may import from WS2_32.dll:
; the import library is made from this list (llvm-dlltool -k), and
; tools/win9x_check.py fails a linked image that imports anything else.
;
; Each name here is exported by name and implemented by the WS2_32 (Winsock
; 2.2) of Windows 98 Second Edition and of Windows Me: the Berkeley calls,
; gethostbyname (no getaddrinfo: Windows XP), and the WSA calls the
; platform layer makes (WSAIoctl's SIO_UDP_CONNRESET is refused on 9x,
; harmlessly). Imported by name: the Windows SDK's ws2_32.lib imports most
; of these by ordinal.

LIBRARY WS2_32.dll
EXPORTS
__WSAFDIsSet@8
accept@12
bind@12
closesocket@4
connect@12
gethostbyaddr@12
gethostbyname@4
gethostname@8
getpeername@12
getservbyname@8
getsockname@12
getsockopt@20
htonl@4
htons@4
inet_addr@4
inet_ntoa@4
ioctlsocket@12
listen@8
ntohl@4
ntohs@4
recv@16
recvfrom@24
select@20
send@16
sendto@24
setsockopt@20
shutdown@8
socket@12
WSACleanup@0
WSAGetLastError@0
WSAIoctl@36
WSASetLastError@4
WSAStartup@8
